    "created_at": "2016-11-07T15:58:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-07T15:58:54Z",
    "body": "@bzbarsky there's no such thing as \"effective script origin\". It's all origins and you can either do \"same origin\" or \"same origin-domain\" on them.\n\nhttps://github.com/annevk/html-cross-origin-objects/blob/master/lore.txt has the original description from @bholley which says the keys are origins. Which might suggest that simply doing object comparisons here (not even \"same origin\") is fine since the origin object remains identical across `document.domain` setting (it's just a field that changes).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
